      "concern": "The Definition requires density in 'C^m(K) in the C^m norm' for every compact K⊂R^q, but does not define this space or norm when m>0 and K has empty interior. Values on K alone do not determine derivatives; for K={0}, the zero function and x↦x have the same restriction and different first derivatives. Specify the ambient-function/jet convention used by this density premise. The universality proof needs derivative approximation of ambient smooth targets on the output closure.",
