      "concern": "Proofs 1.1–2.1 use classical parabolic stability and classical-to-energy identification for h_m-u*. The Statement imports the sampling theorem's trial-class assumptions without explicitly saying that every admitted h_m is C^{2,1}(Q) and continuous on the closed cylinder. Make this regularity premise explicit; finite Hölder seminorms of the evaluated residual and boundary restriction alone are the sampling theorem's operative assumptions.",
